Goal
Add the missing `timeout` parameter forwarding to the top-level `httpx.stream()`
function so user-provided timeout values are correctly passed through to the 
underlying Client stream instead of being silently ignored.

Files to modify
  • httpx/_api.py

Implementation steps
  1. Step 1: In `httpx/_api.py`, add `timeout=None` (or equivalent default) to 
the `stream()` function signature alongside other keyword arguments like `auth`,
`proxies`, `cookies`, etc.
  2. Step 2: In the body of `httpx/_api.py::stream()`, locate the `Client()` 
instantiation or the `client.stream()` call and add `timeout=timeout` to the 
keyword arguments being forwarded so the user-provided value reaches the 
transport layer.

Tests to run
  $ pytest tests/client/test_client.py -k timeout
  $ pytest tests/ -k stream

Risks
  ⚠  If `httpx/__init__.py` re-exports `stream` with an explicit `__all__` or a 
type-stub re-declares the signature, those locations may need updating to match 
the new parameter, but the primary runtime fix is contained within 
`httpx/_api.py`.

